    <item>
      <headword id="d0e56">caisean (uchd)</headword>
      <description>strip 4 in wide cut of breast of ‘mult’ above the ‘a mhaothain’ (solar plexus) right down to the crotch to enable the butcher to get into the belly cavity.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="d0e65">snàil marag</headword>
      <description>Mixture: oatmeal, suet, salt etc., kneaded inside the cavity made while carcase was still warm. Skin of marag was the anal canal turned inside out and thoroughly washed. Mixture was pressed into anal canal which was kept moist and warm in basin of hot water.</description>
    </item>
